MSVC / clang-cl compatibility patch set for OpenFHE 1.5.1.

Base revision: ed361af22049007db2107e7c69bcff209e8c420d
Generated with: git diff HEAD --ignore-submodules=all  (from the OpenFHE tree)

Apply from the OpenFHE source root:
    git apply patches/openfhe-1.5.1-msvc.patch

Rationale for each change is documented in README.md. In short: OpenFHE
upstream refuses to build with MSVC (`#error` guard) and uses GNU-specific
constructs (`__attribute__((deprecated))` in trailing position, `__builtin_ctz`,
`__int128`). clang-cl shares the MSVC ABI, so the tree is adapted rather than
ported. One change is a genuine correctness fix that matters for this project:
`CiphertextImpl<DCRTPoly>::SetLevel` must cast to
`const CryptoParametersCKKSRNS`, otherwise the shared_ptr destructor frees the
crypto parameters while the context still references them, which corrupts the
heap in CKKS `Encrypt` (0xC0000374).

